Write the preaccept of an inbound call on a goroutine of its own, off whatsmeow's event dispatch.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why: onOffer runs on whatsmeow's event dispatch and wrote the preaccept there, with context.Background(). whatsmeow's socket writes with the socket's own context and not the caller's, so a socket that stops draining held the offer, and every node behind it (messages, call terminations), until the socket closed or whatsmeow's handler escape fired. The call is registered before the write and before the integrator hears of it, so moving the write out changes nothing that depends on its order: the accept is deferred until the peer's mute_v2, which follows the preaccept.

